    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0390",
      "reading_order": 428,
      "section": "Amplifier and Low Pass Filter",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 71.99999999999997,
        "t": 544.38280681,
        "r": 503.9854541199001,
        "b": 511.4877348320329
      },
      "content": "The pressure sensor amplifiers include a high gain differential pre-amplifier, followed by a second stage non-inverting amplifier (U6B) with low gain. A trimming potentiometer (R48) is adjusted to minimize any offset in the impedance of the bridge.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_427",
      "parent_section_id": null,
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_427",
          "title": "Amplifier and Low Pass Filter"
        }
      ],
      "page": 48,
      "chunk_hint": "section_start",
      "semantic_role": "overview",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0391",
      "reading_order": 429,
      "section": "Amplifier and Low Pass Filter",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 71.99999999999994,
        "t": 496.38342701790015,
        "r": 504.02439775899893,
        "b": 463.4883550399329
      },
      "content": "A two-pole filter is used to filter the pressure signals. The first pole is formed by a capacitor (C39, multiplied by 230 due to Miller effect) and a Thevenin resistance (seen at U4-2). The second pole is the RC filter at the ADC input, which is located on the CPU PWA.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_427",
      "parent_section_id": null,
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_427",
          "title": "Amplifier and Low Pass Filter"
        }
      ],
      "page": 48,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
